          "entities": {},
          "text": "My grandfather’s uncle, who lived in Kyiv and worked as a teacher, told a joke in a “company of friends” in 1938. Few days later he was invited to local NKVD office (the predecessor of KGB) to talk. He then disappeared. My great-grandma (his sister) was told months later only - he got 10 years without the right to correspondence for anti-Soviet propaganda. Only in 1950s my grandfather found out that he was shot that same year he was arrested. We don’t know even where exactly and when he was buried\n\nSo fuck off with your gaslighting"
